[COMMENTS]
STATION,Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume. Long term IH/UKCEH research catchment. Natural flow regime. GENERAL: Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume designed by Hydraulics Research Ltd, suitable for streams with steep gradients, heavy sediment loads and high flood/drought flow ratios. Catchment nested within Cefn Brwyn (55008). Primary 15 minute dataset available. STATION HYDROMETRY: Shoal formation common, requiring prompt removal to avoid drowning. Check gauged by c/m, and volumetrically for lowest flows. FLOW RECORD: Daily mean flows replaced from 01/10/1973 to 31/12/2010, and AMAX flows from 01/10/1973 to 01/10/2010 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Responsive regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95.
CATCHMENT,Very wet catchment; drains highest area of Plynlimon upland massif. Composed of Ordovician massive grits (unconfined aquifer maintaining baseflow), slates and Silurian mudstones. Heath on peaty plateau; grassland on free draining slopes (supporting sheep grazing) and mires in valley bottoms.
Qmed Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
Pooling Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
